---
List what the project's extensions may make the host do and this machine's approvals of it

`grants approve` and `grants revoke` change the approvals, kept in the user's consent store (ADR 0335).

Usage: specforge grants [OPTIONS]
       specforge grants <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list     List each capability, its grant here and the project's named roots (the default)
  approve  Approve an extension's scopes on this machine (every scope that needs it when none is named), or a root
  revoke   Revoke an extension's approvals (every scope when none is named), a root's, or the whole project's
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --path <PATH>
          A path inside the project (the nearest directory at or above it holding specforge.json; none: the directory itself, with the default configuration)
          
          [default: .]

      --store
          List every approval the consent store holds, for every project

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format: human or json
          
          [default: human]
          [possible values: human, json]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
